Users are profiles to which you can attribute database-level permissions. They allow you to define permissions specific to each type of database usage. For example, users with an `admin` role can create new databases and users.

USAGE:
  scw rdb user <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  create      Create a user for a Database Instance
  delete      Delete a user on a Database Instance
  get-url     Gets the URL to connect to the Database
  list        List users of a Database Instance
  update      Update a user on a Database Instance

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for user
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw rdb user [command] --help" for more information about a command.
